# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own values.
# .env is git-ignored, so nothing machine-specific gets committed.

# Required. The SEC asks every automated request to identify itself with a name
# and a contact email, and blocks traffic that does not. edgartools reads this
# variable and sends it as the User-Agent header on every EDGAR request.
EDGAR_IDENTITY=Your Name your-email@example.com

# Optional. Where edgartools keeps its HTTP cache. Defaults to your home
# directory if left unset.
# EDGAR_CACHE_DIR=.cache/edgar

# Answer generation, by one of three providers. See "Answering a question" in the
# README.
#
# ollama: a local model, with no account, key or network. Install
# Ollama from https://ollama.com/download, then pull the model:
#   ollama pull llama3.2:3b
# soclaas: NUS SoC's SOCLAAS API, which serves larger open-weight models and
# answers in seconds rather than minutes, reachable without the VPN. It needs a
# SOCLAAS key, below. The hosted app and the demo answer with it.
# mistral: Mistral's API on its free plan, also in seconds, the fallback when
# SOCLAAS is down or a limit is hit. It needs a key from your own account, below.
# Unset means ollama. The app opens on this one, and its sidebar's Answer model
# box can switch to another for a session.
# LLM_PROVIDER=soclaas

# Your own Mistral API key, only read when Mistral is the provider, whether set
# above or picked in the app. Make it with your own account at
# https://console.mistral.ai (API Keys), as "Setting up Mistral" in the README
# describes, then remove the # below and paste it after the = sign. Left
# commented until then, so a key added while a notebook or the app is running
# is still read. Every member uses their own key: never share yours or use a
# teammate's.
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=

# Your SOCLAAS API key, only read when SOCLAAS is the provider. Make it with your
# SoC account at https://soclaas-portal.comp.nus.edu.sg, as "Setting up SOCLAAS"
# in the README describes, then remove the # below and paste it after the =
# sign. Left commented until then, for the same reason as the Mistral key.
# SOCLAAS_API_KEY=

# SOCLAAS only. Where its API is. Unset means its own address,
# https://soclaas-api.comp.nus.edu.sg/v1, which is right for everyone: it is
# here for a proxy, or for pointing the tests at a dead address.
# SOCLAAS_BASE_URL=https://soclaas-api.comp.nus.edu.sg/v1

# Which model answers, as the provider names it. Unset means the provider's
# default in src/rag/constants.py: llama3.2:3b for Ollama, ministral-8b-2512
# for Mistral, qwen3.6:35b for SOCLAAS (its ID, never its "default" alias,
# which can be repointed). With Ollama, pull any model you set here first. It
# is the model for LLM_PROVIDER above: `python -m src.evaluation --provider`
# naming another provider uses that provider's default instead.
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.1:8b

# Ollama only. Where your own Ollama is listening. Everyone runs their own;
# nobody connects to a teammate's. Unset means Ollama's default,
# 127.0.0.1:11434, and 127.0.0.1 is always this computer. Only set it if you
# changed the port Ollama listens on.
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# Ollama only. How many of the model's layers go on the GPU. Unset lets Ollama
# decide, which is right for a capable GPU or a Mac. On a laptop with a small
# GPU (2 GB, such as an MX450), set 0: splitting the model across CPU and GPU
# there was more than four times slower than running it on the CPU alone.
# LLM_NUM_GPU=0
